# Load tools/fixtures/chars/engaged-hostile.sav and park the session at the
# threat-disengage prompt, on purpose, for tools/check_headless.sh step 10
# (bd inc-gjzx).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/engaged-hostile.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/threat-freeze.keys <seed>
#
# The fixture stands one square WEST of an awake, hostile, perceiving bugbear
# (see tools/keys/engaged-hostile-save.keys for how and why). ONE key that
# steps further west leaves the bugbear's threatened square and fires
# src/Move.cpp:941's "You are in a threatened area. Abort, Flee or Disengage?"
# before anything else can happen.
#
# EVERYTHING AFTER THAT KEY IS '.', AND NOTHING ELSE MAY FOLLOW IT. Commit
# f7ff2d7 (bd inc-es62) gave ChoicePrompt highlight navigation: an arrow key
# moves the highlight, ENTER picks whatever is highlighted -- including '?',
# which opens the combat manual at src/Move.cpp:943 and never returns, because
# this script carries no ESC to leave it. '.' is KY_CMD_REST, which is not one
# of ChoicePrompt's choices ("afd?") and not an arrow, ENTER or ESC either, so
# TextTerm::ChoicePrompt (src/Term.cpp:2823-2868) just loops and asks again --
# confirmed by reading that loop, not assumed.
#
# DONE MEANS: the run's last screen contains the literal text
# "Abort, Flee or Disengage".
#
# THE THREE LEADING '.' KEYS: tools/headless.sh:206-232 promotes a run to
# exit 5 (NO GAMEPLAY) when logs/session.log is missing, and src/Main.cpp:240
# writes that file on the FIRST COMPLETED TURN. LEFT as the very first key
# fires the threat prompt (src/Move.cpp:941) before any turn completes, so
# the run never plays a turn and is wrongly promoted to exit 5. Three rest
# keys complete three turns first -- well inside the ~30-rest-key death
# budget measured in tools/keys/death-freeze.keys's header -- then LEFT still
# fires the prompt exactly the same way, because resting in place never
# leaves the threatened square.

. . .
LEFT
. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .

@dump:threat
